Task: Tap-snap exclusion (FR6) — Phase 2, task 2

Summary of changes:
- TownProp gains a required `snappable` flag. createTownGrid sets it from the
  prop KIND (false for parked cars, true otherwise) rather than reading it from
  the map, so a parked car cannot be authored as tappable by accident and every
  prop has to answer the question explicitly.
- The router snaps to the nearest prop that is snappable, using propsWithin's
  nearest-first order. Before this, a tap inside 0.45 of a parked car resolved
  onto the car's centre — a destination inside the car's own body.
- The reading of FR6 chosen, and asserted: exclusion per prop, not a veto on
  snapping. A cone just past a parked car is still the prop the kid meant, so it
  wins when it is the nearest aimable prop even if the car is nearer the tap.

Files created: none.
Files modified:
- src/game/town/townGrid.ts (the flag on published prop data)
- src/game/input/inputRouter.ts (its use)
- src/game/input/inputRouter.test.ts (4 tests, all red first: the router snapped
  to 'parkedSedan-1' before the change)
- src/game/town/parkedCars.test.ts (the data half: parked cars false, every
  other prop true)

Why:
The router is the only place a tap becomes an intent, so it is the only place
the "never target a point inside a car" rule can be enforced. Keeping the flag
on the data keeps the router free of a hard-coded list of car kinds.

